  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Delivery throughput",
      "description": "Webhook deliveries per second, worker -> subscriber. This is the N in the resume claim.\n\nsum() is CORRECT here: each worker pod measures its OWN outbound traffic, so the pods' values are independent and add up. Contrast the queue-depth panels, which must use max().",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(http_client_requests_seconds_count[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "deliveries/sec",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Success vs failure",
      "description": "Delivery outcomes per second, split by Spring's outcome tag.\n\nSUCCESS = 2xx. CLIENT_ERROR = 4xx, which this system treats as NON-RETRIABLE and dead-letters immediately. SERVER_ERROR = 5xx, which is retried with exponential backoff.\n\nA rising SERVER_ERROR line with a flat DLQ means the retry logic is absorbing a subscriber outage, which is the system working as designed rather than failing.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(http_client_requests_seconds_count[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Delivery latency p50 / p95 / p99",
      "description": "Time for one worker->subscriber HTTP POST. The p95 here is the M in the resume claim.\n\nComputed server-side from histogram BUCKETS, which is why sum(...) by (le) appears before histogram_quantile: buckets are counts, and counts add across pods. Micrometer could publish a pre-computed percentile far more cheaply, but percentiles DO NOT AGGREGATE -- the p95 of three pods is not the mean of their three p95s, and no arithmetic recovers the real figure. With 3 workers and a fleet-wide claim, buckets are the only correct choice.\n\nWatch the gap between p50 and p95: an average would sit between them and describe neither.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(http_client_requests_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(http_client_requests_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(http_client_requests_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
