    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "DLQ depth now",
      "description": "Current dead-letter queue depth.\n\n*** max() AND NEVER sum(). *** This gauge does not describe the pod publishing it -- it describes SHARED STATE IN REDIS that every worker reads, so all 3 pods report the same number for one real value.\n\nMeasured on this cluster with a genuine 4-job DLQ: max() = 4, sum() = 12. Wrong by exactly the replica count, and it gets worse as you scale up -- which is precisely when someone is looking at this panel. Nothing in Prometheus can detect it; sum() is the natural default and produces a plausible, confident, wrong answer.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "max(webhook_dlq_depth)",
          "legendFormat": "dlq",
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
